-- title:
--   Strong approximation away from a split place, Eichler order
-- statement:
--   Let $a,b\in\mathbb{Q}$ and let $q'$ be a prime such that $\mathbb{H}=\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ satisfies `IsDefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt a b q'`, i.e. $a<0$, $b<0$, and for every height-one prime $w$ of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ the algebra $\mathbb{H}\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_w$ is a division algebra (every nonzero element is a unit) precisely when $q'\in w$. Let $N$ be a nonzero natural number and $R$ a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of $\mathbb{H}$ which is an Eichler order of level $N$, that is, $R=\Lambda_1\cap\Lambda_2$ for two orders $\Lambda_1,\Lambda_2$ each maximal among orders containing it, with the relative index of $R$ in $\Lambda_1$ equal to $N$. Let $r$ be a prime with $r\neq q'$ and let $v$ be a height-one prime of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ containing $r$ (so $\mathbb{H}$ is split at $v$). Then for every unit $x$ of $\mathbb{H}\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}^{f}$ there exist $\gamma\in\mathbb{H}^{\times}$ and units $g,u$ of $\mathbb{H}\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}^{f}$ such that $u$ stabilises, under multiplication, the additive subgroup generated by the elements $z\otimes\alpha$ with $z\in R$ and $\alpha$ a finite adele integral at every place; the component of $g$ at every height-one prime $w\neq v$, i.e. its image under [`Submodule.finiteAdeleEvalAt`](def/Submodule_LocalBox.html#L36), equals $1$; and $x=\gamma\cdot g\cdot u$, with $\gamma$ embedded diagonally by [`Submodule.finiteIdeleDiagonal`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L43).
--
--   This is the strong approximation theorem of Eichler and Kneser in the form $\widehat{\mathbb{H}}^{\times}=\mathbb{H}^{\times}\cdot\mathbb{H}_v^{\times}\cdot\widehat{R}^{\times}$ for a definite quaternion algebra over $\mathbb{Q}$ ramified at exactly one finite prime $q'$, an Eichler order $R$ of arbitrary level $N$, and a finite place $v$ of residue characteristic $r\neq q'$; unlike the companion version, no lower bound on $q'$ is imposed. It is used to transport finite ideles into the $v$-component, feeding the conjugation statement [`QuaternionAlgebra.IsEichlerOrder.exists_conjByFiniteIdele_finiteIdeleDiagonal_mul_eq_of_squarefree_of_not_dvd_of_ne`](thm.html#QuaternionAlgebra.IsEichlerOrder.exists_conjByFiniteIdele_finiteIdeleDiagonal_mul_eq_of_squarefree_of_not_dvd_of_ne).
-- source:
